  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is a bug that presents itself when you attempt to Return to Home while downloading a VRChat world.\n\nYou can reproduce it quite simply:\n\n1. Go to a world you have not yet downloaded (try a world that is large enough so you have time to interrupt it). Try waiting for it to be at least halfway done downloading before you interrupt it, I find that seems to increase the likelihood of this bug occuring.\n\n2. Click \"Return to Home\" before the download can complete.\n\n3. You may be able to return to your home world (especially if that's where you were prior), but any further content loading is now broken. Even your avatar will probably not load-in. Otherwise you'll get stuck in loading screens. Restarting the client is the only fix.\n\nYou may have to repeat these steps a few times, it's not 100% likely to happen. I find it usually happens on the second attempt.\n\nVideo: https://youtu.be/pRujKt37txQ\nIn this video example I get stuck in the loading screen. However, as I said, it's also possible to load-in to your homeworld, but just be unable to load any more content from there on out.\n\nThe fact that it shows \"0.00B of 0.00B\" downloaded for my own home world which I've obviously already downloaded, yet when going to the VRChat default home world which I hadn't yet downloaded successfully downloads the world but seems to fail to load it tells me... maybe it's an issue in the unpackaging step of the loading process?\nNot sure, but felt it's worth writing a quick report on.\n\nThanks!",
